  "discussion": "No updates are expected this morning, as surf numbers look on track. Surf along north- and west-facing shores will remain at High Surf Advisory level conditions through this evening as the current moderate, north-northwest swell begins to slowly drop today. Offshore NDBC buoy 51101 continues to show northwest swell energy at 7 feet, 15 seconds early this morning. Surf will fall below advisory level by tonight and become small by Wednesday. Another moderate, long period northwest swell arrives Wednesday night and will likely push north and west shore surf back to advisory levels Thursday into Friday. A medium- period swell fills in on Saturday, likely prolonging moderate to large surf action into the weekend. The current moderate, medium period south swell will continue a gradual decline through Tuesday. South shore surf will be tiny through much of the week with little southerly background energy reaching the islands. East-facing shores will see an increase in trade wind swell as strong northeast winds fill in today. Surf along east-facing shores will stay big and choppy as trades sustain through much of the week.",
